        "@value": "nl_NL"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#type": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "article"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#title": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "I dreamt, it was"
      }
    ],
    "http://ogp.me/ns#description": [
      {
        "@language": "en-en",
        "@value": "I dreamt, it was is a feast for the senses. NDT alumni and new associate choreographers Imre van Opstal & Marne van Opstal are back with a raw and emotional new creation, exploring what happens to the body when it becomes addicted to anticipation. We are also joined by brilliant makers Sharon Eyal & Gai Behar and their hypnotising, vulnerable, and groovy SAABA (2021), reworked in a bold, new version for NDT 2.  Read everything about the performance in the online programme book March 26 until June 2, 2026  Amare, The Hague March 26 (premiere), 27, 28 April 23, 24, 25  Practical information about your visit to Amare  Theater Rotterdam April 1  Stadsschouwburg Haarlem April 3  Schouwburg Amstelveen April 4  Parktheater Eindhoven April 7  Maaspoort, Venlo April 8    Stadsschouwburg Utrecht April 10  Zwolse Theaters April 19  Schouwburg Tilburg April 21  Theater de Vest, Alkmaar May 22  Internationaal Theater Amsterdam May 27, 28, 29, 30  Theater aan het Vrijthof, Maastricht June 2 Dancers This performance is danced by NDT 2.  See an overview of all NDT 2 dancers Intermissions This performance contains 1 intermission. The duration is approximately 1,5 hours. Introduction talks NDT provides introduction talks prior to nearly all performances throughout the Netherlands. In half an hour you will be introduced to the company and dive into the world of contemporary dance and NDT's repertoire.  You will find the time and location of the introductions in Amare in the information e-mail prior to your visit. Information about the introductions in other theatres can be found on the website of the theatre in question. View more photos in the gallery"
      }
    ],
